CRISPRidentify downstream modifications, 2026:

- fail-closed model bundle, artifact size, and SHA-256 verification;
- deterministic profile-family evidence in prediction records;
- hierarchy-consistent protein classifications that preserve independent-head
  winners as raw evidence and explicitly mark masked conflicts;
- hierarchy-consistent final cassette classifications after direct-profile or
  architecture classification, with preserved raw claims, normalized gating,
  and an explicit per-run masked-conflict count;
- a type-aware genome evidence gate for subtype-null Type VII candidates, with
  `type_vote_fraction` confidence and `direct_profile_type_aggregation`;
- exact Python/runtime constraints for the supported CRISPRidentify v2
  environment; and
- downstream version 0.1.0.dev0+crispridentify.3.

These changes are not an official upstream CasAndra release.

The bundled classification/profile data cite Makarova et al., Nature
Microbiology (2025), DOI 10.1038/s41564-025-02180-8. The associated reference
release is archived at DOI 10.5281/zenodo.17388109 under CC BY 4.0. CasAndra
transforms the reference material through profile selection and construction,
metadata normalization, negative-profile selection, and a deployment refit.
